[h1]Construction Manager[/h1]
A massive quality of life mod that adds new automation, filters, and map modes, to greatly improve the EU5 construction experience.

[h1]Automation Features[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Auto-Expand Buildings[/b]: When toggled will continue to build new levels of the building when possible. You can toggle it for each building on a per location basis, or enable mass expand for a building, where it will construct as many as possible in all eligible locations.
 [*][b]Auto-Expand RGOs[/b]: Adds new RGO levels in locations where auto-expand is toggled on.
 [*][b]Auto-Upgrade All Buildings[/b]: Upgrades obsolete buildings to their next tier across your country, regardless of whether auto-expand is on for that building.
 [*][b]Auto-Build[/b]: Constructs one-per-location buildings (council halls, libraries, market villages, settlement buildings, infrastructure, and more) in the priority order you choose.
 [*][b]Auto-Food[/b]: Builds food-producing RGOs and food buildings in rural locations, picking the highest marginal food output. Can be enabled on a per location, or through a mass toggle based on your selected criteria (i.e. wheat on a river).
 [*][b]Auto-Urbanize[/b]: Promotes rural settlements to towns and towns to cities each month. Sub-toggles per tier, plus an RGO ignore list (gold, gems, spices, etc.).
 [*][b]Auto-Build Capital[/b]: Constructs your capital-only buildings (royal court, supreme court, war college, admiralty, chancery, parliament, etc.) when conditions allow.
 [*][b]Auto-Grant Town Rights[/b]: Grants enabled town rights to your cities and megalopolises in priority order.
 [*][b]Highly configurable[/b]: Each feature can be enabled or disabled, with many options such as min-control, min-gold, min-discount, etc.
[/list]

[h1]New Filters[/h1]
Custom search filters added to the location and building lists:
[list]
 [*]Tax Base and Wealth (with and without control scaling)
 [*]Building Levels Filled (relative to supported cap)
 [*]Production Efficiency and Building Level
 [*]Food Potential Per RGO Level
 [*]R.G.O. Value
 [*]Number of Locations Per Province
 [*]Attacker Penalty (from terrain)
 [*]Good Migration Candidate (non-city under 30k pops)
 [*]Auto-Expand Enabled / Disabled
[/list]

[h1]Map Modes[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Breadbaskets[/b]: Highlights locations where auto-food is enabled.
 [*][b]Food Potential Per RGO Level[/b]: Colors locations by natural food potential. Factors in rgo, terrain, vegetation, climate, named static modifiers, water access, and assumed-max bonuses from windmill, farming village, and irrigation systems etc. Essentially it shows you the locations with the highest possible food output.
[/list]

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
Requires the [b]Community Mod Framework[/b].

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Save-game compatible.
 [*]Not Ironman/Achievement compatible.
 [*]Integrates with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3601047146]Glorp UI[/url] - Load Glorp UI after/blow Construction Manager
 [*]Load after other UI mods that override the location window if you see conflicts.
[/list]

[h1]Change Log[/h1]
See the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/changelog/$item-id$]Change Notes on the workshop page[/url].

[h1]Credits[/h1]
Originally based on the Location Specialization QoL (Auto-Expand) mod by SilverSkye111 but has since been completely remade with many additional features.
